  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 205 PM EST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\n- Upper Low brings showers and even wet snow tonight\n\nAn upper low moves through followed by push of cold air tonight\nwhich could bring the first snow to the northern forecast area  \nby Friday morning. Above freezing skin temperatures should prevent\naccumulations except for the higher elevations of Osceola and \nClare Counties where a coating of slush is possible. No travel\nimpacts are expected.\n\n- Northerly flow lake effect rain showers Friday\n\nLake effect rain showers in north-northwest flow on Friday will\naffect areas close to Lake Michigan with the highest POPs in\nsouthwest Allegan and western Van Buren Counties. The rain will be\ndiminishing and ending Friday night as shortwave ridging moves in.\nCyclonic flow returns over the weekend but fair weather continues\nas a clipper passes far to the north of Lower Michigan.",
